    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Extent brought under multiple use management planning framework</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2014">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0 ha</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Green Accelerator Lab Initiative launched and operationalised for identification of innovators for mainstreaming biodiversity considerations 
2. Demonstrate pilots for effective waste management in 3 Panchayats 
3. Demonstrate innovative solutions for conservation of Giant Grizzled squirrel within the Protected Areas
4. Analyse gaps in production sectors for mainstreaming biodiversity - Tea, Forestry, Cardamom etc. 
5. Identify atleast 2 value chains and plans developed for diversification of livelihoods of local communities through value addition</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Green Accelerator Lab Initiative anchored under the Kerala Start Up Mission was launched by the Honble Finance Minister, Government of Kerala for promoting innovations in the area of biodiversity conservation and sustainable natural resource management
2. Restoration measures were undertaken for securing the population of the Giant Grizzled Squirrel. Tree ladders have been put across 14 locations in the Chinnar Wildlife Sanctuary, Kerala to protect the species from road kills. 
3. Gaps analysed and recommendations placed for mainstreaming biodiversity considerations in production sector (Tea, Cardamom, Forestry, Tourism and Agriculture)
4. 4 value chains identified ( passion fruit, lemon grass, NTFP products, millets) and plans developed for diversification of livelihoods of local communities through value addition 
5. Systems put in place for decentralized waste management in 6 Panchayats in Munnar landscape</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Green Accelerator Lab Initiative launched and operationalised for identification of innovators for mainstreaming biodiversity considerations 
2 Demonstrate pilots for effective waste management in 3 Panchayats 
3 Demonstrate innovative solutions for conservation of Giant Grizzled squirrel within the Protected Areas
4. Analyse gaps in production sectors for mainstreaming biodiversity - Tea, Forestry, Cardamom etc. 
5. Identify at least 2 value chains and plans developed for diversification of livelihoods of local communities through value addition</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Green Accelerator Lab Initiative launched and operationalised for identification of innovators for mainstreaming biodiversity considerations 

2 Demonstrated pilots for effective waste management in 3 Panchayats
 
3 Established canopy bridges at 14 location in Chinnar WLS to reduce Road kills &amp; proposed at Neriyamangalam to Valara , PSNP, Athirappally.

4 Analysed gaps in production sectors for mainstreaming biodiversity. Few gaps identified through PESTLE analysis are :
a. Lack/ineffectiveness of schemes for conservation
b. Lack of clarity on the role of stakeholders
c. Growing inequality in wages
d. Scarcity of labour due to incapacity of sectors to pay wages
e. Low value addition on products
f. Poor ICT knowledge among production sector personals
g. Lack of maintaining traditional shade trees in tea plantation
h. Lack of certifications on sustainable practices
I. Fluctuation of price 
j. Lack of efficient irrigation facilities
k. Lack of enacting regulatory measures for use of chemicals in production sectors

5. Identified the following 2 value chains:
a) Jaggery: technology was introduced in Kerala through the project and established model plots and a model nursery. Also, the branding and packaging was supported as marketing strategy .
Currently the team is working to set up an eCommerce platform.
b) Vanasree: the project Setup a processing center for Honey along with the marketing &amp; branding for the products.
Also,the project is working to set up an eCommerce platform.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Extension of restoration work in degraded forests to 150 Ha additional area
2.	Operationalise the bio composting facility in Munnar
3.	Initiate the Munnar Green Corridor work
4.	Publish Responsible Tourism Protocols for Munnar Landscape
5.	Launch the tourism websites for Mankulam and Kuttampuzha Panchayaths
6.	Identify at least 3 value chains and plans developed for diversification of livelihoods of local communities through value addition
7.	Demonstration of Green Innovation Fund startups through a workshop
8.	Form landscape level/ state level cell for sustainability of the project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
